 "capsule": "Originating as a frontier county of the Kingdom of León studded with defensive castles (Castilla, \"land of castles\"), Castile won effective autonomy under Count Fernán González in the mid-10th century and was proclaimed an independent kingdom by Ferdinand I in 1037. Ruled thereafter through shifting personal unions and separations with León, Castile pushed the Reconquista southward, capturing Toledo in 1085, until Ferdinand III's 1230 accession joined the two crowns permanently.",
